      "code": "          do { ",
      "explanation": "do-while loops allows you to execute a piece of code several times, while a certain condition is true.do-while loop is the post-condition loop, which means, it first executes the body of the loop and then checks for the terminating condition. Hence, do-while loop will always execute at least once.\r\n"
    },
    {
      "line_no": 5,
      "code": "               System.out.println(\"Count is: \" + count); ",
